cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. The results have not been independently reviewed."
title: "Derived isogenies of ordinary K3 surfaces as a class-group action: a negative result for isogeny-based cryptography"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dare
    given-names: Christopher
date-released: 2026-11-15
version: "1.0-draft"
license: [MIT, CC-BY-4.0]
repository-code: "https://github.com/chris-dare-dev/k3-derived-isogenies"
keywords:
  - K3 surfaces
  - complex multiplication
  - class group action
  - isogeny-based cryptography
  - CSIDH
  - abelian fourfolds
  - derived equivalences
abstract: >-
  Does the CM class-group action on ordinary K3 surfaces over finite fields,
  through twisted derived equivalences, give a new hard problem for
  cryptography? In the six-line family (Picard number 16) it does not: it
  reduces to a CSIDH-type class-group action on abelian fourfolds with
  multiplication by Z[i], with a group of about 0.01 q^2 elements, steps that
  cost about l^4, and one bit leaking through a quadratic character for about
  one polynomial in six. Notes, scripts and a ledger that recomputes every
  headline number from the stored results.
